<title>USA: Thailand buys 24,000 T U.S. wheat - trade.</title>
<headline>Thailand buys 24,000 T U.S. wheat - trade.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand bought a total of 24,000 tonnes U.S. wheat early this week slated for first half April shipment, several exporters said.</p>
<p>The wheat was divided into three lots out of which 11,550 tonnes was U.S. dark northern spring, 4,000 tonnes hard red winter and 8,500 tonnes western white wheat, one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>The business was done on Monday night, he said.</p>
<p>Prices were not disclosed.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
